music oooh ha ha da romantic  relationships seem pretty simple in the  fairytales I grew up watching boy meets  girl boy likes girl and girl likes boy  boy marries girl and they live happily  ever after  maybe the prince has to slay a dragon  first but after he rescues the girl they  inevitably fall in love with each other  however as we grow up and get older we  realized that romantic relationships are  nowhere near that simple I'm a longtime  fan of Shonen anime anime filled with  epically cool characters who might pick  their nose but man can they kick ass  when the chips are down Shonen was  definitely the first runner I got into  through stuff like Dragon Ball Z and  then eventually Naruto and Inuyasha  obviously I never stopped loving epic  battles but I eventually developed a  love for romance and anime - Inuyasha  had some of it with a love triangle  between Inu Yasha Kagome and kikyo and  that was one of the things that really  drew me to the show yeah there was no  shortage of blood and gore but there was  also a focus on the complicated  relationship between Kagome and Inuyasha  who was still haunted by kikyo I liked  that it wasn't simple it wasn't a pure  and straightforward love you'd get in  the old fairy tales I grew up watching  Inuyasha had feelings for Kagome but he  also still had feelings for his first  love kikyo a relationship wasn't just  the reward at the end of a big battle it  was a constant battle in and of itself  love can be as complicated and messy as  war eventually gravitated to romance  anime like Clannad after story and honey  and clover that acknowledged how  complicated relationships could be  Clannad is not about a brave hero who  comes in slays the dragon and marries  the perfect girl it's about a guy with  issues and a girl with issues helping  each other work through their issues and  enjoying some beautiful but fleeting  moments of happiness in the process then  cut out after story complicated things  even further clown afte